217 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/Alt(Figure 1. Study design. \(1\) Laboratory kicks recorded with optical motion capture provide the ground truth \(shown: a CMU ball kick, fading poses up to ball contact\). \(2\) A virtual broadcast camera films each kick from five views at five player sizes and 25 or 50 fps \(insets: the same instant at 200, 80 and 50 px\), and its exact 2D projections are corrupted with the residuals that a detector makes on real broadcast shots; real video with synchronised capture \(MoVi\) and a digital twin of each recording test the simulation. \(3\) The 2D keypoints are lifted to 3D with MotionAGFormer, with official or kick-adapted weights. \(4\) Six kinematic features and three swing-leg joint moments are compared with the laboratory \(bias, mean absolute error, limits of agreement, ICC with the classes of Koo and Li\), and an illustrative sensitivity analysis considers how independently established measurement reliability could affect injury-study size.)/K[28]/P 51 0 R/Pg 6 0 R>>
endobj

